.page gapsh-builtins 7 the builtin commands of gapsh

# DESCRIPTION
Builtins run inside the shell itself. A few of them (`echo`, `true`, `false`, `kill`) also exist as separate programs in `/bin`; the builtin is used when a name is typed. `type NAME` tells which is which. A function or alias of the same name hides a builtin; `command NAME` runs the builtin or program regardless.

# THE BUILTINS
    :  true  false            do nothing; succeed; fail
    echo  printf              write text
    cd  pwd  pushd  popd  dirs
                              directories
    exit  return  break  continue
                              leave things
    export  readonly  unset  local  set  shift
                              variables and arguments
    alias  unalias  type  command
                              names and how they resolve
    source  .  eval  exec     run code
    read                      read a line
    test  [                   conditions
    jobs  fg  bg  wait  kill  processes
    trap                      run something at exit; ignore signals
    history  umask  ulimit  getopts  help

Each has a page of its own, for example `patchouli cd`.

# SEE ALSO
gapsh(1), gapsh-language(7)
